    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">35-1703.02910v1_rag::chunk_005</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">103-2210.12704v1_rag::chunk_008</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">49-1904.00370v3_rag::chunk_005</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">59-2022.findings-emnlp.80_rag::chunk_002</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">113-2111.02275v2_rag::chunk_006</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">60-2022.findings-emnlp.235_rag::chunk_006</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the acquisition function must be simple to compute and optimize (e.g., distance to classication hyper-plane) because it will be used by the generative model during the sample generation process</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To decide what data points to acquire though we used MC dropout following the derivations above. We repeated the acquisition process 100 times, each time acquiring the 10 points that maximised the acquisition function over the pool set.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">We focus on using epistemic uncertainty to identify the most informative points for label acquisition. Bayesian Active Learning by Disagreement (BALD) [ 18 ] denes an acquisition function</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">an acquisition function A measuring the information gain of a potential data point x</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">where a ( x , M ) is the acquisition function</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the 10 points that maximised the acquisition function over the pool set</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To decide what data points to acquire though we used MC dropout following the derivations above.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">a data point from the unlabeled set U is selected to be labeled, according to an acquisition function A measuring the information gain of a potential data point x</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">maximizes the acquisition function (2) . It is often the case that a single example will not cause a signicant change of the model posterior</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">an acquisition function a ( x, M ) is a function of x that the AL system uses t</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Bayesian Active Learning by Disagreement (BALD) [ 18 ] denes an acquisition function based on epistemic uncertainty.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">a variety of acquisition functions, such as predictive entropy and Bayesian Active Learning by Disagreement (BALD)</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">using an acquisition function to be annotated by the oracle such that the expected loss is minimized.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Active learning research focuses on developing novel acquisition functions for selecting data points to be annotated by the oracle.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A random acquisition function selects data points uniformly at random from D pool and adds them to D train .</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">unifying the uncertainty and diversity objectives into a single acquisition function</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">acquisition functions, such as predictive entropy and Bayesian Active Learning by Disagreement (BALD) (Houlsby et al., 2011), can be calculated and optimized to query new examples in active learning.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#pool_based_active_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#deep_active_learning"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Pool-based Active Learning</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A scenario where the active learning algorithm selects the most useful samples from an accessible pool of unlabeled data.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0005</hasCQ>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0020</hasCQ>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0052</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0005</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0020</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0052</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">26-2009.00236v2_rag::chunk_004</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">51-1910.07153v2_rag::chunk_000</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">40-1702.07956v5_rag::chunk_003</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">AL approaches can be divided into membership query synthesis [ 10 , 113 ], stream-based selective sampling [ 41 , 118 ] and pool-based [ 131 ] AL</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In pool-based active learning, accessible unlabeled data are not used for model training in most conventional metho</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">it aims to select the most useful samples from the unlabeled dataset</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Another commonly used poolbased active learning principle is uncertainty sampling.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#acquisition_time">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#acquisitionfunction"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Acquisition Time</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The time required to select samples, which impacts the interactive experience of active learning loops.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0219</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0219</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">60-2022.findings-emnlp.235_rag::chunk_010</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">reducing the acquisition time is crucial to the interactive experience of the active learning loops.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#learnsfrom">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#model"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#training_data"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">learnsFrom</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The relationship where a model acquires knowledge from specific data increments.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0111</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0111</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">30-2210.04137v2_rag::chunk_014</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">a model (often a neural network) learns from training data</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#trainingiterationcount">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
