  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#aggravates">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#class_imbalance"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#cold_start_problem"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">aggravates</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The relationship where the distribution of classes negatively impacts the initial selection bias or representativeness of the model.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0147</hasCQ>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0200</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0147</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0200</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">127-1909.03585v1_rag::chunk_010</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the cold start problem can be further aggravated. Treating samples of all classes equally often leads to selecting samples that are likely to be similar</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#model_training_step">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#model"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Model Training Step</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A discrete step in the active learning process where the model is updated or retrained.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0233</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0233</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">111-2023.findings-acl.697_rag::chunk_007</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the number of annotated samples added in each model training step for all AL baselines.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#stoppingcriterion">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#method"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">StoppingCriterion</rdfs:label>
    <skos:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Stopping Criterion</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A general mechanism or condition used to terminate the active learning process, involving aspects such as metrics, datasets, and conditions.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0007</hasCQ>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0059</hasCQ>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0082</hasCQ>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0104</hasCQ>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0183</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0007</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0059</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0082</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0104</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0183</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">177-2005.07402v1_rag::chunk_011</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">177-2005.07402v1_rag::chunk_010</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">15-2210.10109v2_rag::chunk_014</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">25-mathematics-11-00820_rag::chunk_027</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">With a stopping time of t determined by a certain criterion, we consider as a measure of goodness for the stopping criterion.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The proposed stopping criterion is also applicable to other active learning frameworks</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">For the design of a general stopping criterion, there are three main aspects to consider: metric , dataset and condition</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In the active learning technique, the query process continues until a stopping condition is met.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">We describe a specic algorithm for stopping active learning with a GP.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/S0/R1#addedto">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#label"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/S0/R1#dataset"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">addedTo</rdfs:label>
    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The action of moving a sample into the labeled set after a label is acquired.</skos:skos_definition>
