    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">46-Gong Deep reinforcement active 2020 Accepted_rag::chunk_003</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">At each iteration, an active learning algorithm has two stages: 1. identifying a set of data-points and presenting them to an oracle to be labelled, and 2. training a classier</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Active learning (AL) combines data labeling and model training to minimize the labeling cost by prioritizing the selection of high value data</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">allows the algorithm to interactively query the human annotator with the instances recognized as the most informative samples</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
