    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">26-2009.00236v2_rag::chunk_006</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The paper explains AL scenarios, query strategies, the analysis of different active learning techniques</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Active learning aims to select the most important data from the unlabeled dataset and query human experts to annotate new data.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The query strategy, such as uncertainty sampling, is usually used to score the candidate instances in the pool.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Uncertainty-based query strategy refers to the model based on sample uncertainty ranking to select the sample to be queried.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A taxonomy of query strategies for AL.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The batch-based query strategy forms the basis of the combination of AL and DL</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">although the hybrid query strategy achieves superior performance, the uncertaintybased AL query strategy is more convenient to combine with the output of the softmax layer of DL.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The query strategy based on uncertainty is an important direction of AL research.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
