    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">constructing representations for all data points in the unlabeled data pool</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">randomly select one or more samples from the unlabeled pool</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">X U denotes a much larger pool of samples ( x U ) which are not yet labeled.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">we can randomly select one or more samples from the unlabeled pool</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">select the most informative samples from the unlabeled pool D U</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the predictive entropy of unlabeled data instances that were selected from the unlabeled pool.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">estimate acquisition factors ( e.g. , condence) for remaining unlabeled data U</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">a data point from the unlabeled set U is selected to be labeled</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">constructing representations for all data points in the unlabeled data pool and/or executing clustering on the pool.</hasEvidenceText>
